  "title": "Stabilize Birkhoff tangent projections near permutation matrices",
  "body": "## Problem\n\nTangent projection can become numerically invalid at strictly positive doubly stochastic matrices close to a permutation matrix. The fixed-gauge constraint system is ill-conditioned there, and solving its normal equations squares that condition number. Even a zero vector can be projected to a large non-tangent value, corrupting natural gradients and optimizer steps.\n\nFor a double-precision 2-by-2 matrix with off-diagonal entries `1e-8`, the existing projection has an error of about `0.08` against the analytic Fisher-metric projection. Solving the same system with QR reduces that error below `3e-9`.\n\n## Change\n\nSolve the existing rectangular least-squares system with the QR-based `gels` driver instead of forming and solving `B.T @ B`. Fixing the existing gauge makes the system full column rank in the strictly positive interior.\n\nThe gauge, projection formula, batch handling, and least-squares interpretation for approximately doubly stochastic inputs are preserved.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe tests use the analytic Fisher projection for 2-by-2 matrices and an independent tangent-basis Gram solve for larger interior matrices. They exercise natural gradients, tangent and zero-vector preservation, broadcasting, noncontiguous inputs, empty batches, differentiation with respect to both inputs, and real RiemannianSGD updates checked against analytic natural gradients. An SVD-based oracle checks the retained least-squares semantics for approximately stochastic inputs.\n\nOn both Python 3.8 / PyTorch 2.0.1 CPU and Python 3.12 / PyTorch 2.8.0 CPU:\n\n- The unchanged implementation produces **19 failures and 8 passing controls**, without collection errors or skips.\n- All **27 new cases** pass with the fix. The complete regression, Birkhoff, Birkhoff-geometry, manifold-basic, Riemannian-SGD, and Adam modules report **2183 passed, 310 existing skips**.\n- Production and regression Ruff checks, `git diff --check`, and the clean-source check pass.\n\n[Baseline and fixed CI results](https://github.com/Afloat16/geoopt/actions/runs/43674701216). The verification workflow is on a separate fork branch.\n",
  "prefilled_url": "https://github.com/geoopt/geoopt/compare/master...Afloat16:fix/birkhoff-projection-conditioning-20261115?expand=1&title=Stabilize%20Birkhoff%20tangent%20projections%20near%20permutation%20matrices&body=%23%23%20Problem%0A%0ATangent%20projection%20can%20become%20numerically%20invalid%20at%20strictly%20positive%20doubly%20stochastic%20matrices%20close%20to%20a%20permutation%20matrix.%20The%20fixed-gauge%20constraint%20system%20is%20ill-conditioned%20there%2C%20and%20solving%20its%20normal%20equations%20squares%20that%20condition%20number.%20Even%20a%20zero%20vector%20can%20be%20projected%20to%20a%20large%20non-tangent%20value%2C%20corrupting%20natural%20gradients%20and%20optimizer%20steps.%0A%0AFor%20a%20double-precision%202-by-2%20matrix%20with%20off-diagonal%20entries%20%601e-8%60%2C%20the%20existing%20projection%20has%20an%20error%20of%20about%20%600.08%60%20against%20the%20analytic%20Fisher-metric%20projection.%20Solving%20the%20same%20system%20with%20QR%20reduces%20that%20error%20below%20%603e-9%60.%0A%0A%23%23%20Change%0A%0ASolve%20the%20existing%20rectangular%20least-squares%20system%20with%20the%20QR-based%20%60gels%60%20driver%20instead%20of%20forming%20and%20solving%20%60B.T%20%40%20B%60.%20Fixing%20the%20existing%20gauge%20makes%20the%20system%20full%20column%20rank%20in%20the%20strictly%20positive%20interior.%0A%0AThe%20gauge%2C%20projection%20formula%2C%20batch%20handling%2C%20and%20least-squares%20interpretation%20for%20approximately%20doubly%20stochastic%20inputs%20are%20preserved.%0A%0A%23%23%20Validation%0A%0AThe%20tests%20use%20the%20analytic%20Fisher%20projection%20for%202-by-2%20matrices%20and%20an%20independent%20tangent-basis%20Gram%20solve%20for%20larger%20interior%20matrices.%20They%20exercise%20natural%20gradients%2C%20tangent%20and%20zero-vector%20preservation%2C%20broadcasting%2C%20noncontiguous%20inputs%2C%20empty%20batches%2C%20differentiation%20with%20respect%20to%20both%20inputs%2C%20and%20real%20RiemannianSGD%20updates%20checked%20against%20analytic%20natural%20gradients.%20An%20SVD-based%20oracle%20checks%20the%20retained%20least-squares%20semantics%20for%20approximately%20stochastic%20inputs.%0A%0AOn%20both%20Python%203.8%20%2F%20PyTorch%202.0.1%20CPU%20and%20Python%203.12%20%2F%20PyTorch%202.8.0%20CPU%3A%0A%0A-%20The%20unchanged%20implementation%20produces%20**19%20failures%20and%208%20passing%20controls**%2C%20without%20collection%20errors%20or%20skips.%0A-%20All%20**27%20new%20cases**%20pass%20with%20the%20fix.%20The%20complete%20regression%2C%20Birkhoff%2C%20Birkhoff-geometry%2C%20manifold-basic%2C%20Riemannian-SGD%2C%20and%20Adam%20modules%20report%20**2183%20passed%2C%20310%20existing%20skips**.%0A-%20Production%20and%20regression%20Ruff%20checks%2C%20%60git%20diff%20--check%60%2C%20and%20the%20clean-source%20check%20pass.%0A%0A%5BBaseline%20and%20fixed%20CI%20results%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FAfloat16%2Fgeoopt%2Factions%2Fruns%2F43674701216).%20The%20verification%20workflow%20is%20on%20a%20separate%20fork%20branch.%0A",
